remstart
    THE STEAM DEMO
    the free demo on Steam is this same game, built with -p:FishSteamDemo=true (Fade.MonoGame.csproj). the
    Steam workflow makes one beside the full game, and uploads it to the demo's own app (steam/SETUP.md,
    "The demo"). Program.cs reads the build back and sets FISH_STEAM_DEMO, and setup_steam_demo sees it. a
    Debug run with FISH_STEAM_DEMO=1 is the demo too.

    it is not THE DEMO of fish_headers_demo, which is the game playing itself on the main menu. that one
    is in the demo too, and in the full game.

    the demo is the whole game, for STEAM_DEMO_ROUNDS rounds. every kind of game can be started, and a short
    one is over before the demo is, so it can be won. any other game stops when that many rounds have been
    won: the bar fills, and in place of the upgrade screen the page of THE END OF THE DEMO comes up over the
    game, with the store page of the full game, in the Steam overlay, and "Done". the Rounds Left on the
    screen counts down to the end of the demo, and so does what the angler says about them.

    THE SAVE IS SHARED. the demo keeps its prefs.json where the full game does (Program.cs, the save
    directory), and Steam Cloud carries it from the one app to the other (steam/SETUP.md). so a player who
    buys the game has the tutorial seen, their options, the codec and everything else that was found, and the
    game of the demo is there to carry on with: it was saved with the round won, so the full game carries on
    with the upgrade screen of that round. the demo carries it on too, but only as far as the end page.
    every save says which of the two made it (PREF_SAVE_DEMO). a player who has the full game and opens the
    demo has a saved game that the full game made, and the demo leaves it alone: there is no Resume for it,
    and the demo never saves over it, nor forgets it. see steamDemoHandsOff.

    the demo has no achievements (achieveOk) and sends no scores to the leaderboards, which are the full
    game's. its high scores are kept on the machine, as they always are.

    what the rest of the game does for it:
    - fish.fbasic does `gosub setup_steam_demo` before anything is set up
    - frame_score asks steamDemoStops() when a round is won, and the main loop does
      `gosub handle_steam_demo_over`, beside handle_game_end
    - save_game, forget_saved_game and hasSavedGame ask steamDemoHandsOff()
    - showRoundsLeft and the angler's line about the rounds use steamDemoRoundsLeft()
    - logoFrame calls steamDemoTag(), which makes the tag the first time, and logoHide hides it
remend

global STEAM_DEMO = 0 `1 in the demo
` how many rounds a game of the demo has. (no comment on the line of a #constant: it becomes part of the number.)
#constant STEAM_DEMO_ROUNDS 10
global STEAM_DEMO_OVER = 0 `1 when the last round of the demo has been won, and 2 while its page is up
` the store page of the full game. the demo is an app of its own, so this is not its own page.
global STEAM_DEMO_STORE_URL$ = "https://store.steampowered.com/app/5416340/"

` which of the two made the saved game: 1 the demo, 0 (or never set) the full game
#constant PREF_SAVE_DEMO 23
global dim STEAM_DEMO_TEST_PREFS(3) `what fish_tests_steamdemo makes the preferences say. a global dim in a test file is never made.

` the tag beside "Pop", on the main menu
global STEAM_DEMO_TAG_ID = 0
global STEAM_DEMO_TAG_X# = 132 `from the middle of the logo, before it is scaled: beside "Pop", to the right
global STEAM_DEMO_TAG_Y# = 30
global STEAM_DEMO_TAG_ANGLE# = -.32
` how long after "Pop" it comes in
#constant STEAM_DEMO_TAG_WAIT 420
